  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Contributing to the decrease in morbidity and mortality due to tuberculosis by the year 2014 in accordance with the stop TB Partnership and the Millennium Development Goals - Madagascar (01-Jul-2012-31-Mar-2016)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Malagasy population is estimated to be 18.8 million, spread over 22 regions and 111 health care districts. The prevalence of all forms of TB was estimated at 415 per 100,000 in 2006. The program supported by this grant aims to reduce the rate of TB in the population by maintaining the detection rate above 70 percent; increasing the rate of treatment success from 76 percent to a minimum of 85 percent by 2014; and halving TB prevalence by 2015 with respect to 1990 levels. The program will focus on key populations that are most at risk of TB infection, including: populations in remote and poor areas; prisoners in the country&amp;#39;s 30 largest penitentiaries; and people living and working in mining and extraction zones. The program will also support people suffering from multidrug-resistant TB in 20 priority areas.</narrative>
  </description>
